KG42.register("clusters-2b03afba161cd2540834d6a6",{"id":"04-energy_collectives::v142-d-K004","paper":"04-energy_collectives","label":"Conditional selection of collective interface objectives and supervision of optimality","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"Conditional selection of collective interface objectives and supervision of optimality","market_meaning":"The community manager selects an interface objective according to the collective's common agreement and supervises collective optimization subject to overall convexity being maintained. The market-driven, autonomy, largest-importer, intertemporal peak-shaving, and geographical-preference branches are separately applicable examples and are not automatically added together into a single objective.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"R011 and R012 express different functional perspectives on the same supervisory responsibility, with R012 explicitly retaining the convexity condition. R013 encapsulates multiple cases in the same frozen chain, and each branch retains its own conditions; scalars, time vectors, and the two types of upper-bound variables are not equated unconditionally.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The common rule in this cluster concerns interface model selection and its admissibility conditions for optimality, rather than joint implementation of all cases. The corresponding branches are referenced in dedicated clusters for largest-importer settlement consequences and three-neighborhood allocation, preventing all mechanisms from being conflated into a single rule on the basis of the manager node.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Provides the manager's responsibility to supervise the convergence of community clearing."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"primary","role":"alternative","rationale":"Retains the collective-optimum perspective on the same supervisory responsibility and the explicit convexity condition; it is not counted as an additional independent supervision rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R013","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Represents interface selection, common fairness criteria, and the examples of conditional objectives; preserves the boundaries between cases within the chain."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-C01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"The same source passage links optional interface models with optimality supervision and restricts admissible models through overall convexity; the supervisory responsibility is not interpreted as a guarantee that an arbitrary numerical algorithm will converge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-C02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R011","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"The two chains originate from the same supervisory statement and are assigned to allocation and collective-objective functions, respectively; the latter explicitly adds a convexity qualification, so the link is retained without unconditional deduplication."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R011::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R012::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R013::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R013::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"References to the same M02 manager in model selection and supervision; unified display does not merge the two distinct clearing function nodes."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M02","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19"],"rationale":"Candidate representations of the same supervisory responsibility, but the frozen constraints differ in how explicitly they state the conditions; both original assertions are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M03","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C005","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C008"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g02-e05"],"rationale":"The source presents the largest-importer objective and its epigraph formulation as corresponding representations; the applicable coefficients and the conditions for the upper bound to be tight still require clarification, and they are not treated as two independent penalty rules."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-M04","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C006","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C009"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g02-e07"],"rationale":"The peak objective across time periods and its upper-bound formulation are candidate representations of the same peak-shaving branch; the time vector and coefficient conditions are retained, and this branch is not conflated with the branch for maximum imports by a member."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G01","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R013 reuses the q_imp, q_exp, γ_imp, and γ_exp objects to represent both scalars and T-dimensional vectors, and the same vartheta object represents upper bounds on both the maximum member import and the temporal peak. These local roles cannot be combined into a single generic quantity.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::x::v141-c-R013-x-q-imp","v141-c-R013::x::v141-c-R013-x-q-exp","v141-c-R013::x::v141-c-R013-x-theta","v141-c-R013::theta::v141-c-R013-th-gamma-imp","v141-c-R013::theta::v141-c-R013-th-gamma-exp"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Have C specify the dimensions, indices, and local identities of upper-bound objects by branch; D uses only references restricted to particular branches, leaving the existing objects unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The signs of the penalty coefficients and the conditions for epigraph variables to be tight are unspecified. Negative weights may destroy the convexity of norm objectives, and zero weights do not guarantee that the upper bound equals the maximum; the convexity of the norm itself cannot directly guarantee the applicability of all branches.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C001","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C004","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C005","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C006","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C008","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the parameter signs, feasible regions, correspondence of optimal values, and conditions for upper bounds to be tight in each branch, and specify the range of admissible models; no numerical values or constraints that were not provided may be added."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G03","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"In Eq. (5) of the autonomy branch, only q_imp appears on the left-hand side, whereas the right-hand side involves q_exp; the explanation of Eq. (6) uses γ_e rather than γ_exp. Questions also remain about the N3 balance in the geographical branch, so the entire model family cannot be regarded as mathematically closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C004","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g01-E30","v141-b-g02-e10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the function arguments, coefficient subscripts, and complete balances for the three neighborhoods; the specific closure gap in the geographical branch is also retained in v142-d-K006."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G04","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R013 combines different economic purposes and temporal and spatial conditions within a single chain that cannot be split or modified; at present, its primary assignment can only be to the selection rule, with specified branches referenced in other clusters.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C003","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C004","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C005","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C006","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E20","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g01-E29"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If independent retrieval of the complete rules for each case is subsequently required, have C establish branch boundaries and dedicated objects in a new version; do not split and rewrite the frozen chain in this round or assume that all objectives are enabled simultaneously."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G05","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The interface objective and fairness criteria still lack independently approved objects. Both the interface model proposal and the collective fairness criteria proposal remain pending; fairness criteria cannot be equated with social welfare or price.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R012","v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R012::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R013::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E28","v141-b-g02-e04"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-P01","v141-b-g02-prop-01","v141-b-g01-P02"],"required_work":"Manually review the conceptual boundaries between the entity, the interface objective, and distributive fairness criteria; retain only proposal references until approval and revision by C."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G06","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence for model selection, supervision, and all objective examples has not undergone independent review; this cluster is only an experimental candidate.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011","v141-c-R012","v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E19","v141-b-g01-E21","v141-b-g01-E24","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g01-E30"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently, manually check the complete sources and parameter conditions, continuing to retain unverified status and the gaps identified in this round."}]},"rule_refs":["04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R011","04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R012","04-energy_collectives::v141-c-R013"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["KG31-2f18db99132618b2","KG31-3fa7c9f6716d2240"]});
